A||||5||Cooter||How can you test or check a turbo?||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||10-28-2000||06:45 PM||||A Saturday afternoon in the junkyard and I find a 80something T-Bird turbo coupe. The price was right and I left with the turbo and intercooler (I will go back for the hood vents later- they will be sold in the mall for what ever I pay for them).<BR>How can I determine if the thing needs to be rebuilt or not? It spins free and the shaft has no wobble to it. Doesn't appear to have been leaking oil in the intake or exhaust side. Any ideas? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tom88gt||10-28-2000||07:24 PM||||It sounds like you just completed the test.  Looks like you found a good turbo.  If you have a mechanics stethascope, you can check the bearings more closely just to be sure. ||||reg||12
Z||000002||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-29-2000||12:30 AM||||Cooter....   Sold....  I'll buy the setup of what ever you have found as soon as you get them.... Let me know how much $$$ to send you...  (903)825-7744  You can even call collect.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||10-29-2000||05:19 PM||||Cooter, I have the same turbo and inter-cooler (not installed). Got it from an 87 T-Bird. It's an IHI unit, but might be a bit small. I haven't found the trim for the blades yet, but I think it's around .52 on the turbine... too small. I may be wrong and I hope I am because mine is real good condition.<P>Let me know if you find the A/R for the turbine and the trim for the compressor, OK?||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||10-29-2000||05:23 PM||||If you take off the exhaust housing (behind the wastegate... the part with the O2 bung in it) you can inspect the turbine and spin the wheel to see if it spins freely. Then take a peek in the other end to inspect the compressor blades. If the wheels spins freely and the blades aren't chipped, missing, bent...etc. you should be OK. A rebuild kit is less than a 100 bucks though.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||10-29-2000||07:17 PM||||Thanks for all the replies and info!<BR>1FieroGT- I am keeping my turbo, but the front hood vents from the T-bird were what I was talking about selling. If that is what you meant, you have first call on them. I believe they would look nice in the front hood of our cars if you turn them backward to let out air under the hood.<BR>Today I found another one of these turbos. Hmm if one is too small, I wonder how one on each bank would do. . .||||reg||1
